[{"id":3551612051,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7TsUyT","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"209899834712c664d27e9b4b3200e401ccecdfc1","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","login":"AdriaandeJongh","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh"},"body":"Tried it and it works (love it!!!) but there's two caveats:\r\n\r\n- many functions show two zones in the profiler, an 'outer' and an 'inner'. Ideally these would be one zone, but this isn't a blocker for this PR in my opinion.\r\n<img width=\"1762\" height=\"695\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-12-08 at 11 55 00\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f212ff3-87f9-4191-a04f-6dd27f8dcb75\" />\r\n\r\n- the function line numbers are not correct: the 'outer' function zones incorrectly show the line number of the function they're being called from, whereas the 'inner' function zones correctly show the line number of the called function. An example:\r\n<img width=\"1191\" height=\"1267\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-12-08 at 11 39 05\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8118a772-5879-4801-b1d5-e9859e2d3588\" />\r\n<img width=\"1030\" height=\"312\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-12-08 at 11 38 11\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b602134-86b9-45cd-904d-f27b6b491dc4\" />\r\n<img width=\"972\" height=\"332\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-12-08 at 11 38 18\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce22f14c-915c-45f7-8ab2-ffc6267f612f\" />\r\n<img width=\"940\" height=\"379\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-12-08 at 11 38 22\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a2e379f-5192-4766-b32e-b1ba76dc990d\" />","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113632#pullrequestreview-3551612051","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113632","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-12-08T11:43:48Z"},{"id":3559264525,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7UJhEN","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"209899834712c664d27e9b4b3200e401ccecdfc1","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?u=4a42fd867f2c449fcc23adf635dd574dae98e6c2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","login":"akien-mga","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga"},"body":"Code looks good to me, and this was tested in production by Adriaan.\r\n\r\nTo clarify why we merge a new feature after feature freeze: this finalizes the work on the Tracy profiler integration which was done in 4.6, so we decided to make an exception to the feature freeze for it.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113632#pullrequestreview-3559264525","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113632","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-12-09T19:14:28Z"}]